{
  "name": "callback-parameters-after-used",
  "description": "A function used as a value may be passed more arguments than it declares, so a callback's unread parameter is reported for deletion only when no parameter after it is read, and an unread parameter before the last read one is reported for a rename to an underscore name, unless its name has one. A function whose signature is free has every unread parameter reported but one whose name starts with an underscore, which declares it unread. A name an object binding pattern of a callback's parameter binds that the body never reads is reported for deletion at probable, because the pattern reads the property it names from the argument and the code handing the argument may act on that read. A declared function's parameter that destructures its argument is judged by the names it binds: each unread name is reported, except a name beside a rest element of the same object pattern. A rest parameter is judged as the last parameter, and a this parameter receives no argument and is never reported.",
  "languages": [
    "ts"
  ],
  "target_kind": "application",
  "expect": [
    {
      "symbol": "Unused",
      "report": "none"
    },
    {
